### Modern certs + cert-manager plan (tick boxes as you complete)

How to use this checklist
- Tick each box when done to track progress. Replace `[ ]` with `[x]` (or click the checkbox in the editor).
- Aim for the bare minimum to meet goals. Prefer sensible defaults; expose options only where necessary.
- Keep scripts simple, portable Bash; follow the repo's Bash-ninja standards and avoid over-engineering.

---

## Phase 0 — Preconditions and guardrails
- [ ] Ensure `openssl` and `bash` are available at runtime. If missing, print a friendly error and exit.
- [ ] Add strict mode to all scripts under `src/`: shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, then `set -Eeuo pipefail`, `IFS=$'\n\t'`, and `umask 077` for key material.
- [ ] Add traps: `trap 'on_err $LINENO' ERR` and `trap 'on_sig' SIGINT SIGTERM` with minimal handlers printing concise errors (no secrets).
- [ ] Implement global option parsing once (quiet/verbose/no-color/non-interactive/help), reusable by subcommands (see `Bash-ninja rules`).
- [ ] Implement `.env` loader with precedence: CLI > env > .env > defaults.

Files likely touched
- [ ] `src/main.sh` (single entrypoint; subcommands `init`, `issue`, `eject`, `re-init`, `validate`, `version`, `help`)
- [ ] `src/common.sh` (shared helpers for parsing, logging, dotenv, path helpers)

Definition of done for Phase 0
- [ ] `bash -n src/*.sh` passes
- [ ] `shellcheck src/*.sh` has no errors of severity error

---

## Phase 1 — Modernize certificate generation (avoid `-legacy`)
- [ ] Default key type to EC P-256 (`KEY_TYPE=ec`, `EC_CURVE=prime256v1`); allow `KEY_TYPE=rsa` with `RSA_BITS>=3072`.
- [ ] Replace legacy keygens with `openssl genpkey` everywhere (root, intermediate, server).
- [ ] Store keys in PKCS#8; when encrypting, use PBES2 + AES-256 and PBKDF2 with configurable iterations.
- [ ] CSR: use `-sha256`; add SANs via `-addext "subjectAltName = ${SERVER_SANS:-DNS:${SERVER_CN}}"`.
- [ ] Signing: `openssl ca -batch -md sha256 -days ${LEAF_DAYS:-398}`; default `LEAF_DAYS=398`.
- [ ] PKCS#12 export: use AES and SHA-256 (no legacy provider): `-keypbe AES-256-CBC -certpbe AES-256-CBC -macalg sha256 -iter ${PFX_ITER:-204000} -maciter`.
- [ ] PKCS#8 conversion for app-consumed server key: `openssl pkcs8 -topk8 -v2 aes-256-cbc -iter ${PKCS8_ITER:-204000}`.

Files likely touched
- [ ] `src/init.sh` (root/intermediate keygen → genpkey; keep sha256; respect KEY_TYPE and defaults)
- [ ] `src/request-server-cert.sh` (server keygen → genpkey; SANs; -batch signing; PKCS#8 and PKCS#12 options)

Quick verification (no `-legacy` expected)
- [ ] `openssl x509 -noout -text -in <server>.cert.pem | grep -E "Signature Algorithm|Subject Alternative Name"`
- [ ] `openssl verify -CAfile ca-chain.cert.pem <server>.cert.pem`
- [ ] `openssl pkcs12 -in <server>.pfx -nodes -passin pass:"$PASS" -info >/dev/null`
- [ ] `openssl pkcs8 -in <server>.pkcs8.key.pem -passin pass:"$PASS" -nocrypt -out /dev/null`

---

## Phase 2 — OpenSSL config cleanup
- [ ] Remove deprecated `nsCertType` and `nsComment` from `src/openssl-*.cnf`.
- [ ] Ensure `default_md = sha256` and `copy_extensions = copy` (already present for intermediate).
- [ ] Server extensions present: `keyUsage = critical, digitalSignature, keyEncipherment` and `extendedKeyUsage = serverAuth`.

Files likely touched
- [ ] `src/openssl-root.cnf`
- [ ] `src/openssl-intermediate.cnf`

---

## Phase 3 — Command model and UX
- [ ] `src/main.sh` dispatches subcommands; unknown subcommand → help + exit 2; `help` or empty → usage + exit 0.
- [ ] Each subcommand has its own `parse_<cmd>_opts` and `run_<cmd>` following the portable `getopts` long-option mapping via `-:`.
- [ ] Global flags honored by all subcommands: `--help`, `--quiet`, `--verbose`, `--no-color`, `--non-interactive`.
- [ ] Add `--version` printing git tag/commit when available.

---

## Phase 4 — Dockerfile hygiene (minimal but pinned)
- [ ] Base: pin to a small image (e.g., `alpine:3.20`). Avoid `:latest`.
- [ ] Install pinned OpenSSL (e.g., `apk add --no-cache openssl=~3.1 bash`).
- [ ] Non-root user, executable scripts, and minimal entrypoint.

Files likely touched
- [ ] `Dockerfile`

---

## Phase 5 — Local Dockerized tests (no CI)
- [ ] Provide a local-only test runner script: `scripts/test-local.sh` (do not add CI workflows).
- [ ] The script runs inside Docker to ensure a clean, reproducible env:
  - [ ] Build or reuse a minimal image with `bash`, `openssl`, and `bats` (either reuse main `Dockerfile` or create a temporary container that installs `bats`).
  - [ ] Run `bash -n src/*.sh` and `shellcheck src/*.sh` inside the container.
  - [ ] Run a smoke test: init → issue → verify chain; assert no `-legacy` required for PKCS#8/PKCS#12.
  - [ ] Cover `--non-interactive` path; fail clearly if a required passphrase is missing.
- [ ] Document usage in `README`: `./scripts/test-local.sh` (no network/CI dependencies).

Files likely touched
- [ ] `scripts/test-local.sh`
- [ ] `test/smoke.bats` or `test/smoke.sh`
- [ ] Optional: `docker/Dockerfile.test` if not reusing the main image

---

## Phase 6 — cert-manager export subcommand (Issuer)
Goal: export artifacts/manifests so Kubernetes cert-manager can use the intermediate CA as a CA Issuer. Do NOT change existing CA layout.

- [ ] Implement `simpleca cert-manager export` subcommand.
- [ ] Options (portable `getopts` with long mappings):
  - [ ] `--ns|--namespace` (required)
  - [ ] `--issuer-name` (default `ca-issuer`)
  - [ ] `--secret-name` (default `ca-key-pair`)
  - [ ] `--out` (default `/opt/export/manifests`)
  - [ ] `--crl` (repeatable)
  - [ ] `--ocsp` (repeatable)
  - [ ] `--force` (allow overwrite)
- [ ] Export unencrypted PKCS#8 intermediate private key into export dir ONLY (never modify `/opt/ca`).
- [ ] Build full chain: `intermediate.cert.pem + root/ca.cert.pem` → `issuer.fullchain.crt.pem`.
- [ ] Render `secret.yaml` with base64 (no wraps): `type: kubernetes.io/tls`, keys: `tls.crt` (full chain), `tls.key` (unencrypted intermediate key).
- [ ] Render `issuer.yaml` that references the Secret; include optional `crlDistributionPoints` and `ocspServers` arrays when provided.
- [ ] Print clear warning that an unencrypted key is written; treat export dir as sensitive.
- [ ] Validation: verify chain, and that intermediate pubkey parses; optional YAML syntax check if `yq` present.

Files likely touched
- [ ] `src/cert-manager.sh` (parse + run)
- [ ] `src/common.sh` (paths: `rootCaCert`, `intermediateKey`, `intermediateCert`, `certificateChain`)

Quick verification
- [ ] `openssl verify -CAfile <root>/ca.cert.pem <intermediate>.cert.pem`
- [ ] `base64 -w0` used for both key and chain in manifests
- [ ] `kubectl apply -f <out>/<ns>/<issuer-name>/secret.yaml` (manual env) succeeds

